{"attempt_id": "attempt:um-kou-21.70-kourovka-notebook-problem-21.70-0407926d-source-fidelity-01", "created_at": "2026-09-06T08:00:00Z", "graph_id": "graph:um-kou-21.70-kourovka-notebook-problem-21.70-0407926d-v1", "obligations": [{"acceptance": {"allowed_candidate_kinds": ["proof", "counterexample", "formalization", "computation"], "required_capabilities": ["human_review", "statement_faithfulness"]}, "dependencies": ["obligation:um-kou-21.70-kourovka-notebook-problem-21.70-0407926d-statement-fidelity"], "kind": "root_claim", "obligation_id": "obligation:um-kou-21.70-kourovka-notebook-problem-21.70-0407926d-root", "source_refs": ["https://www.unsolvedmath.com/problems/KOU-21.70"], "statement": {"formal_declaration": null, "language": "en", "text": "A group $G$ is called an orientable Poincar\\'e duality group of dimension $n$ over a ring $R$ if it is of type $FP$ over $R$ and $H^i(G;RG)=0$ for $i\\ne n$, while $H^n(G;RG)=R$ as an $RG$-module, where the action on $R$ is trivial. (Note that $G$ is not required to be finitely presented.) If $G$ is an orientable Poincar\\'e duality group of dimension $n$ over all fields, is it an orientable Poincar\\'e duality group over the integers?"}, "statement_sha256": "0b89c77675db97a22836cc74bcf0ec62056fc59574c28db8c8caa9f9aacee39c"}, {"acceptance": {"allowed_candidate_kinds": ["proof"], "required_capabilities": ["human_review", "statement_faithfulness"]}, "dependencies": [], "kind": "definition", "obligation_id": "obligation:um-kou-21.70-kourovka-notebook-problem-21.70-0407926d-statement-fidelity", "source_refs": ["https://www.unsolvedmath.com/problems/KOU-21.70"], "statement": {"formal_declaration": null, "language": "en", "text": "Verify against the cited source that the frozen statement is complete, current, untruncated, attribution-correct, and unambiguous enough for mathematical research; record any definition or quantifier gap without silently editing the contract."}, "statement_sha256": "65f0b3d574bd6d837403149dab6434c0f5